Section 3 of 14 — Overall assessment
# 1. Overall Assessment

## 1.1 Verdict

**The strategic conclusions of Missions 001A and 001B are directionally
plausible but not justified by the evidence presented.**

The two reports converge on a defensible high-level instinct: sell services now,
build institutional capability over time, position on governance. That instinct
is probably correct. But the reports do not *establish* it, and several of their
specific, actionable, prioritized recommendations are contradicted by their own
internal evidence or are operationally infeasible.

The gap is not primarily a research-effort gap. It is a **reasoning-discipline
gap**: the documents assemble a large volume of market-level and funding-level
context, then attach prioritized recommendations to it without an explicit
inferential bridge. Rankings are published without a ranking function. Confidence
is asserted globally rather than derived per claim. Constraints — money, hours,
credentials — are never introduced, so nothing in either document can be
infeasible, and therefore nothing is excluded.

